---
title: Lasagna
servings: 8
tags: [italian, pork, make-ahead, weekend]
cuisine: italian
time: 2 hours 15 minutes
source: Classic Lasagna by Jennifer Segal, Once Upon a Chef, https://www.onceuponachef.com/recipes/classic-lasagna.html
---

== Sauce ==

Pulse the @yellow onion{1}(roughly chopped), @garlic{5%cloves},
@carrots{2}(roughly chopped) and @celery{1%stalk} in a #food processor{} until
finely minced but not a purée.

Heat @olive oil{2%tbsp} in a #large pot{} over medium-high heat. Add the
@italian sausage{1.5%lb}(bulk, or out of its casings) and cook ~{5%minutes},
breaking it up, until lightly browned but not cooked through. Lift it onto a
plate.

Add another @olive oil{1%tbsp} and turn the heat to medium. Cook the minced
vegetables ~{7%minutes} until very soft, without colouring them.

Pour in the @red wine{3/4%cup}(dry) and scrape up the browned bits. Cook a few
minutes until most of it has gone.

Add the @crushed tomatoes{28%oz}, @heavy cream{1/2%cup}, @salt{3/4%tsp},
@black pepper{1/4%tsp}, @sugar{2%tsp}, @dried thyme{1.5%tsp} and @bay leaves{2}.
Bring to a boil, then cover and simmer ~{20%minutes} until thick.

Chop the sausage smaller and return it to the pot. Cover and simmer
~{10%minutes} until cooked through. Season to taste and take out the bay leaves.

== Ricotta filling ==

In the food processor, blend the @ricotta{15%oz}(whole milk),
@cream cheese{3%oz}, @eggs{1}, @garlic{1%clove},
@parmesan{3/4%cup}(Parmigiano-Reggiano, grated), @salt{3/4%tsp} and
@black pepper{1/4%tsp} until even. Add the @basil{1/2%cup}(roughly chopped) and
pulse until it is finely chopped.

== Assembly ==

Heat the oven to 375°F (190°C).

Spread about 1 1/2 cups of the sauce over the bottom of a
#9x13-inch baking dish{}. Lay 3 of the @dried pasta{12}(oven-ready no-boil lasagna noodles)
on top, leaving small gaps between them.

Spread a third of the ricotta filling over the noodles and scatter on 3/4 cup of
the @mozzarella{16%oz}(shredded whole milk). Repeat sauce, noodles, ricotta and
mozzarella twice more.

Lay on the last 3 noodles, spoon over the rest of the sauce, and top with the
rest of the mozzarella and @parmesan{1/4%cup}(Parmigiano-Reggiano, grated).

Cover tightly with foil, greased side down, and bake ~{40%minutes}. Uncover,
raise the oven to 400°F (205°C), and bake ~{20%minutes} more, until bubbling and
golden at the edges.

Rest ~{15%minutes} before cutting.

> The noodles soften in the sauce, so leave gaps between them; they swell to
> fill the dish.
